      ":question/id": "ab0fcf96-043b-5b3c-b205-f7fd3df937b7",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+z &=4 \\\\ y-z &=-4 \\\\ z &=1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nNotice that the matrix $M$ is already in row echelon form.\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\nR_{2}:=R_{2}+R_{3},\\qquad M\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\n$$\nR_{1}:=R_{1}-R_{3},\\qquad M\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 1\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=3 \\\\ y &=-3 \\\\ z &=1\\end{aligned}\\right..\n$$\n\nSo, we have the solution $x=3$, $y=-3$, and $z=1$.",
